      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "With 4 mana, I'm weighing Sold Out on Momo against Day of Black Sun at X=2, which would kill Momo and my Official but leave Ruffians, Engineer, and Peddlers untouched since they're MV3 — X=3 would be needed for those but costs 5 mana.\n\
\n\
Actually, I realize DoBS strips abilities before death, so Momo's exile trigger wouldn't fire — that makes X=3 next turn a clean sweep of their board (Momo, Ruffians, Engineer) plus my two small creatures, while I keep Tundra Tank since it's not a creature. That's tempting, but delays my Combustion Man and Ran and Shaw curve, and I'll take another 3 in the air this turn dropping me to 13. Leaning toward playing Tundra Tank now and casting DoBS X=3 next turn.\n\
\n\
I considered instead playing Tank now and holding DoBS for next turn, but that trades away my two creatures while they keep attacking with Momo. Sold Out now keeps my two deathtouchers back to defend, which is cleaner, so I'll go with Sold Out.\n\
\n\
