      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "I'm at 3 life against a flying 6/4 Ruffians, an unblockable 2/2 Spirit, and a 2/3 Engineer — enough incoming damage to kill me next turn, so I need to figure out how to block or stop this lethal swing.\n\
\n\
Considering Day of Black Sun X=2 to wipe the Spirit token, but that also kills my own Court Official while leaving Ruffians and Peddlers untouched, and I'd have no reach blocker for the flyer afterward. Casting Yuyan Archers to block Ruffians instead seems better, but the unblockable Spirit still drops me to 1 life, and I don't have enough mana left to do much else that turn.\n\
\n\
I'm also weighing which card to discard to Archers' ETB when I need to dig for a land — Combustion Man is a durable 4/6 blocker but dies to 6 power, while Ran and Shaw's 4/4 flying body could trade with Ruffians but also dies to it, so neither discard feels safe with only four lands and no land in hand.\n\
\n\
As for attacking, I think it's better to hold back rather than trade Peddlers or send Official into Engineer, since I need blockers more than early damage right now, and Tundra Tank's stats are too unclear and it can't stop a flyer anyway.\n\
\n\
I'll go with Archers instead. Cast it and hold the remaining 2 mana since Prison's activation needs 4, which I don't have.\n\
\n\
